    "Use a complete feed labelled for adult laying hens. A useful planning baseline is about 115 g per hen daily; real intake varies with breed, temperature and production. Follow the feed label and monitor body condition. Do not give high-calcium layer feed to growing chicks. Keep fresh water available.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Use a complete feed labelled for adult laying hens. A useful planning baseline is about 115 g per hen daily; real intake varies with breed, temperature and production. Follow the feed label and monitor body condition. Do not give high-calcium layer feed to growing chicks. Keep fresh water available."
          }
        },
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Für erwachsene Legehennen ein entsprechendes Alleinfutter verwenden. Etwa 115 g pro Henne täglich sind ein Planungsrichtwert; Aufnahme hängt von Rasse, Temperatur und Legeleistung ab. Futteretikett beachten und Körperzustand prüfen. Küken kein kalziumreiches Legefutter geben. Stets frisches Wasser anbieten."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Utilisez un aliment complet pour pondeuses adultes. Environ 115 g par poule et par jour servent de base ; la consommation varie selon la race, la température et la ponte. Suivez l’étiquette et surveillez l’état corporel. Ne donnez pas d’aliment riche en calcium aux poussins. Laissez de l’eau fraîche disponible."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Use ração completa para poedeiras adultas. Cerca de 115 g por galinha ao dia é uma base de planejamento; o consumo varia com raça, temperatura e postura. Siga o rótulo e observe a condição corporal. Não dê ração rica em cálcio a pintinhos. Mantenha água fresca disponível."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Weekly eggs": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Weekly eggs"
          }
        },
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Eier diese Woche"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Œufs de la semaine"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ovos da semana"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Wheezing, repeated sneezing, discharge, reduced appetite or unusual quietness need attention. Separate an unwell bird, provide water and contact a poultry veterinarian. Breathing difficulty or sudden deaths require urgent advice. A journal cannot identify the cause; do not choose medicines from symptoms alone.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Wheezing, repeated sneezing, discharge, reduced appetite or unusual quietness need attention. Separate an unwell bird, provide water and contact a poultry veterinarian. Breathing difficulty or sudden deaths require urgent advice. A journal cannot identify the cause; do not choose medicines from symptoms alone."
          }
        },
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Röcheln, häufiges Niesen, Ausfluss, Appetitverlust oder ungewöhnliche Ruhe beachten. Kranke Vögel absondern, Wasser anbieten und einen Geflügeltierarzt kontaktieren. Atemnot oder plötzliche Todesfälle sind dringend. Ein Tagebuch erkennt keine Ursache; Medikamente nicht allein nach Symptomen wählen."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Respiration bruyante, éternuements répétés, écoulements, perte d’appétit ou calme inhabituel demandent de l’attention. Isolez l’oiseau, fournissez de l’eau et contactez un vétérinaire aviaire. Difficultés respiratoires ou morts soudaines sont urgentes. Un journal ne détermine pas la cause ; ne choisissez pas de médicament sur les seuls symptômes."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Chiado, espirros repetidos, secreção, falta de apetite ou quietude incomum merecem atenção. Separe a ave doente, ofereça água e contate um veterinário de aves. Dificuldade para respirar ou mortes súbitas exigem orientação urgente. O diário não identifica a causa; não escolha remédios só pelos sintomas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
